Fillets: a corner of three roundings in the layout of a torus corner (the
corner's own face a plane normal to the pivot's guide) whose two sides
have different radii is the torus of the larger radius round the pivot;
past its section on the smaller side it runs on up to where it crosses the
smaller rounding's blend, which ends there (mitcad#2091).

Defect. A block standing on a plate, its vertical edge rounded 5 and the
two foot edges at that corner 0.8 and 1. Expected: the torus of radius 1
round the rounding of 5 (ring 6, tube 1), the rounding of 1 meeting it at
its section, the rounding of 0.8 meeting it where the two blends cross;
the material the union of the blends' fills. Observed: the corner was
walked with a radius running from 0.8 to 1 along a circle
(BRepBlend_EvolRad), a free-form face 0.39 mm3 short of the fills' union.
ToricCorner takes a torus only for equal radii, and the pivot meets each
side at that side's own radius from the face (0.8 and 1 up the rounding of
5), so the pivot's two section parameters differ, which the test for a
torus refused as well.

- PerformThreeCorner: in that layout (ToricLayout, ToricCorner's test less
  the radii) with radii more than tolapp3d apart, the pivot a cylinder and
  its points at the sides' own radii from the face (within tolapp3d), the
  corner is ComputeCorner's torus of the larger radius, its section on the
  smaller side taken on the pivot at the larger radius as on the other.
- unequalTail: past that section the torus runs on (the tail) into W, the
  face the smaller rounding shares with the pivot, which cuts it, up to its
  crossing with the smaller rounding's blend. The crossing runs from P3,
  where the torus's contact on the corner's face meets the smaller
  rounding's, to P2, where the smaller rounding's contact on W meets the
  torus's cut by W; both as intersections of the contacts' curves on their
  faces. The cut and the crossing are GeomInt_IntSS curves of windows of
  the surfaces round the corner (a period less 0.05 wide in a periodic
  direction, so that no seam splits them), moved into the corner's periods.
  A branch is the cut or the crossing where its curve passes within ten
  times the intersection's reached tolerance (or ten tolapp3d) of the
  points found on the faces: the curves are approximations within that
  tolerance, the points exact on the contacts. The tail is a corner stripe
  of its own on a copy of the torus, from the crossing to the section,
  which it shares with the corner (regular there); the smaller rounding
  ends at the crossing (no regularity: the blends cross at an angle). The
  tail's transitions on the corner's face and on W are the smaller
  rounding's there, turned where the tail runs the other way.
- Where P3 or P2 is missing (beyond the section within a quarter turn of
  the torus, in the smaller rounding's range, inside its faces) or no
  branch is found, the torus is removed from the data structure and the
  corner is walked as before. A box's three convex edges (the torus's
  contact on the top curving away from the smaller rounding's) are such a
  case, and so is a side whose contact on the corner's face ends at an
  edge of that face short of P3.
Concave sides round a convex pivot, and their complement (convex sides
round a concave pivot, the same blends), give the volume of the fills'
union and of the box less it within 1e-5 mm3, either side the smaller,
radii from 0.5 and 2 to 0.9998 and 1. Equal radii and radii within
tolapp3d keep their ways.

Upstream: new.
Test: geometry.fillet_unequal_torus_corner.

